{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":24,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 24:1"},"Why, seeing times are not hidden from the Almighty, do they that know him not see his days? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 24:2"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Some"]}," remove the landmarks; they violently take away flocks, and feed ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["thereof. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 24:3"},"They drive away the ass of the fatherless, they take the widow’s ox for a pledge. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 24:4"},"They turn the needy out of the way: the poor of the earth hide themselves together. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 24:5"},"Behold, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as"]}," wild asses in the desert, go they forth to their work; rising betimes for a prey: the wilderness ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["yieldeth"]}," food for them ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," for ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["their"]}," children. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 24:6"},"They reap ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["every one"]}," his corn in the field: and they gather the vintage of the wicked. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 24:7"},"They cause the naked to lodge without clothing, that ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["they have "]},"no covering in the cold. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 24:8"},"They are wet with the showers of the mountains, and embrace the rock for want of a shelter. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 24:9"},"They pluck the fatherless from the breast, and take a pledge of the poor. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 24:10"},"They cause ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["him"]}," to go naked without clothing, and they take away the sheaf ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["from"]}," the hungry; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 24:11"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Which"]}," make oil within their walls, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," tread ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["their"]}," winepresses, and suffer thirst. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 24:12"},"Men groan from out of the city, and the soul of the wounded crieth out: yet God layeth not folly ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["to them. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 24:13"},"They are of those that rebel against the light; they know not the ways thereof, nor abide in the paths thereof. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 24:14"},"The murderer rising with the light killeth the poor and needy, and in the night is as a thief. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"JOB 24:15"},"The eye also of the adulterer waiteth for the twilight, saying, No eye shall see me: and disguiseth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["his"]}," face. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"JOB 24:16"},"In the dark they dig through houses, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["which"]}," they had marked for themselves in the daytime: they know not the light. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"JOB 24:17"},"For the morning ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," to them even as the shadow of death: if ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["one"]}," know ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["them, they are in"]}," the terrors of the shadow of death. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"JOB 24:18"},"He ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," swift as the waters; their portion is cursed in the earth: he beholdeth not the way of the vineyards. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"JOB 24:19"},"Drought and heat consume the snow waters: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["so doth"]}," the grave ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["those which"]}," have sinned. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"JOB 24:20"},"The womb shall forget him; the worm shall feed sweetly on him; he shall be no more remembered; and wickedness shall be broken as a tree. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"JOB 24:21"},"He evil entreateth the barren that ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["beareth"]}," not: and doeth not good to the widow. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"JOB 24:22"},"He draweth also the mighty with his power: he riseth up, and no ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["man"]}," is sure of life. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:22"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"23","sid":"JOB 24:23"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Though"]}," it be given him ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["to be"]}," in safety, whereon he resteth; yet his eyes ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," upon their ways. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:23"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"24","sid":"JOB 24:24"},"They are exalted for a little while, but are gone and brought low; they are taken out of the way as all ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["other,"]}," and cut off as the tops of the ears of corn. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:24"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"25","sid":"JOB 24:25"},"And if ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it be"]}," not ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["so"]}," now, who will make me a liar, and make my speech nothing worth? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 24:25"}]}]}
